WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.178 --> 00:00:02.140
- Well, Alison, you're doing a guest role

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:03.270
on "Days of Our Lives".

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:05.840
So is this, I mean, you just had,

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:07.940
you were this character
for so long, right?

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.920
And then is it weird to go
back after all these years?

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:12.590
- Yeah, it started when I was 16.

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:13.590
I mean, I played
- Wow.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:15.530
this character more than half of my life.

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:17.570
- Wait, just a minute, think about that.

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:20.120
Your boy is 16.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.860
You have been this
character since you were,

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:22.890
can you imagine your kid?

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.510
I always think back to
like things like that,

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:25.630
and I'm like, oh my God.
- Oh my god, right,

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:26.673
at his age, this is how old
- Yeah.

00:00:26.673 --> 00:00:28.880
Yeah.
- I was when I auditioned,

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:30.480
oh my gosh, I hadn't,

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:31.560
Kelly, I hadn't even thought of that.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:32.653
Yes, I was his age
(man laughs)

00:00:32.653 --> 00:00:34.440
when I auditioned to play this part.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:35.273
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:35.273 --> 00:00:36.870
- And I remember at the
time thinking it would be

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.650
like one day a week, you know,

00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:41.010
kids on soap operas aren't on very often.

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:43.090
And I wasn't even supposed
to be acting anymore.

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:46.120
I had told my dad I
really should just stay

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.620
around casting directors,
you know, so don't forget me.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:50.570
But he was really focused on my education

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:51.720
and wanted me to go to college.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:55.890
And so he's sort of unwillingly
agreed to one more audition.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:57.220
And it was for "Days
of Our Lives" (laughs).

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:59.760
And I got the job.
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.000
I can't imagine.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:01.833
Oh my go--
- No, I know.

00:01:01.833 --> 00:01:02.820
That's what I think about things,

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:04.890
like even me moving across
country on my own at 18

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:07.810
living on a mattress, in this
like nothing like little room.

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:10.610
Like I can't imagine
letting my kid do that.

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:11.600
Like there's things I did

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:12.790
that I'm like what?
- Right.

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:13.623
- Like, yeah,

00:01:13.623 --> 00:01:14.470
but it's interesting,
- Yeah.

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:16.560
- like you've been there
since 16 years old.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:17.393
And so is it,
- And I (indistinct)

00:01:17.393 --> 00:01:18.226
- I heard you've been gone

00:01:18.226 --> 00:01:19.320
for like--
- work on time

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:20.820
and know all my lines
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:21.890
- and be responsible.

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:23.880
And you know, part of
growing up in this industry

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.680
is that kids, you know,

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:27.170
even if you're a kid, they don't care.

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:28.710
You have to know your lines,
you have to be prepared,

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:31.100
you have to do it again 70
times if that's what they say.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:34.360
Like, I remember one director
telling me, you know,

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.610
my laugh wasn't realistic
enough when I was like eight.

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:39.060
I had this like fake laugh,

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:41.410
and he made, he was
not kidding by the way,

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:43.280
he didn't try to make me laugh for real.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:46.690
Like he laid into me, and
I had to go into my trailer

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:51.000
and figure out how to laugh
fake but make it sound real.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.270
And I was so,

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:53.649
I remember being terrified.
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:53.649 --> 00:01:54.482
At eight?
- Like you better

00:01:54.482 --> 00:01:56.370
get this right sweetie, pull it together.

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:57.530
Yeah.
- Yeah at eight,

00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:59.630
nah, I was like, still like,

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:02.567
I was doing nothing like
what you were doing, wow.

